# Husky hooks and shell scripts must keep LF endings: they are executed by
# /bin/sh on the Linux runners, where a trailing CR makes `set -e` fail with
# "set: Illegal option -" (this broke the release workflow's metadata commit).
#
# The committed blobs must be LF too: with `eol=lf`, a CRLF blob is checked out
# as LF, so `git diff` compares LF against CRLF and reports the file as modified
# forever. `git reset --hard` cannot fix that, which blocked the release
# workflow's rebase ("You have unstaged changes", exit 128). Keep blobs
# normalized with `git add --renormalize .` after changing eol rules.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
.husky/** text eol=lf
